{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>All that YHWH did to Pharaoh and to Egypt on Israel's account.</b> As one who repays vengeance upon the enemies of his people, in the manner of אָשִׁיב נָקָם לְצָרָי (Deuteronomy 32:41) — and this through what He inflicted upon their bodies at the sea, as it says: יְשַׁלַּח בָּם חֲרוֹן אַפּוֹ עֶבְרָה וָזַעַם וְצָרָה מִשְׁלַחַת מַלְאֲכֵי רָעִים (Psalms 78:49). By this He demonstrated that He chose Israel as His treasured possession above all peoples." "<b>All the hardship that found you on the way.</b> Through hunger, thirst, and the war of Amalek." "<b>And YHWH delivered them.</b> By this He demonstrated His particular providence over them — the cause of which necessarily follows from their convictions and deeds being properly directed to serve Him with one accord."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:26:05.129864529Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}